        {
          "text": "October 06, 2023 at 2:59 pm",
          "url": null,
          "urls": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Hi Pai,",
          "url": null,
          "urls": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Would this work with already cooked fish bones (if the fish was minimally seasoned and had a little bit of tomato with it anyway)? Also, I notice in the video you seem to have just bought cut up bones, or else there are no instructions on how to prepare the bones for cooking… I have some fish heads; I’ve seen (only after I cooked them) that in some cases, such as for Ara-jiru (Japanese fish bone soup) that the heads are de-gilled, and cut in half and gutted. As I cooked my fish whole, I didn’t do this… would some bitter flavours come out in my stock, do you think?",
          "url": null,
          "urls": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Thanks in advance for your answer (hopefully)!",
